{
  "format": "sfxgen/1",
  "name": "Footsteps: puddles (loop)",
  "description": "Rubber boots walking slowly through shallow puddles on a street: a loop of eight steps, no two alike. Each step: the boot comes down through the water onto the asphalt with a dull thud that the water mostly hides, and the flat of the sole hits the surface a moment later. The water answers with a wet splash: a dense crackle of tiny pops of drops and bursting skins, each a very short ring, through a resonance that moves as the water sloshes, densest at first and quickly thinning, with a soft edge of mist over it, only a sprinkle of bigger bubbles, and a small \"shlop\" under it as the water is shoved aside and falls back. Then the thrown water plips back into the puddle drop by drop, thinning to the odd last drop, and as the boot lifts a few small drops fall off it. The puddles differ: some are barely wet, the deepest gulps with fat bubbles, and only some steps drip. Speed goes from a slow, careful wade to a run through standing water.",
  "tags": [
    "footstep",
    "footsteps",
    "steps",
    "loop",
    "water",
    "puddle",
    "splash",
    "rain",
    "wet",
    "walk",
    "run",
    "foley"
  ],
  "duration": 7.7066,
